## S2 FAIL-ONLY demonstration (V28 vs pre-fix tree)

V28 MUST be FAIL-ONLY pre-fix (spoof succeeds on the unpatched tree) and
PASS post-fix. Demonstrated two ways (recorded 2026-10-28, Refs #9):

(a) Dynamic — `scripts/send_identity.py` moved out of the tree (pre-fix
shape), `./scripts/verify-rigs.sh --check-only` run, file restored
byte-identical after. Result: exit 1,
`SUMMARY: 35 checks passed, 4 failed`, with exactly these V28 lines:

- `[FAIL] V28/09-send-identity: cannot load scripts/send_identity.py
  ([Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../scripts/send_identity.py')`
- `[FAIL] V28/09-send-identity: scripts/send_identity.py unreadable
  ([Errno 2] No such file or directory: '...')`
- `[FAIL] V28/09-send-identity: tests.test_send_identity failed:`
  (corpus import error — module absent; no secret material in output)

plus the expected S1-layering cascade
(`[FAIL] V23/107-identity: tests/test_identity_m1.py failed:` — its S1
fixture imports the attestation module). Unbound-role renders are
unaffected (the render import is lazy: bound roles only). Full failing
output retained in scratch (`/tmp/v28-failonly3.txt`, scratch-only).

(b) Static — the true pre-fix tree (spec base 4b453a2) additionally lacks
the S1 render block and the S0 evidence file, so V28's remaining checks
fail there too (verified read-only, no worktree mutation):

- `git show 4b453a2:scripts/render-seat.py | grep -c
  "send-identity.json|sender_binding_filename"` → `0` (each render-marker
  check calls `fail()`)
- `git show 4b453a2:scripts/send_identity.py` → `fatal: path
  '.../send_identity.py' exists on disk, but not in '4b453a2'`
- S0 evidence `docs/evidence/09-send-identity-spoof.md` committed in S0
  (51228f3), absent at base → `fail()` on the evidence checks.

Post-fix: `SUMMARY: 36 checks passed, 0 failed` with
`[PASS] V28 send-identity attestation (09-send-identity S1) green:
binding rules + !cat render + 24 corpus tests pass + S0 evidence present`.

